# Copy this file to .env, in this same folder, and fill in what you need. Everything here is optional: a public
# Loom link needs none of it. A variable already set in your shell wins over this file. .env is git-ignored.

# --- Private recordings -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Loom that is not shared by link needs Loom's session cookie (`connect.sid`; copy it from loom.com >
# DevTools > Application > Cookies; it lasts about 30 days). Give it one of two ways.

# 1. Keep it in 1Password and name the item here. The item needs a field labelled `connect.sid`. It is read
#    when you run `source scripts/loom_cookie.sh` before a command, so the cookie never touches the disk.
#LOOM_OP_ITEM="Loom session"

# 2. Or paste the cookie itself. Simpler, but it sits in this file in plain text.
#LOOM_COOKIE='s%3A...'

# --- Project-specific identifiers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A JSON file of identifiers to spot in the narration (see "Project-specific identifiers" in SKILL.md). Named
# here it applies everywhere and takes priority over a project's own .loom-context.json.
#LOOM_CONTEXT_CONFIG=/path/to/entities.json
